  "id": "Compound::DB00777 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Propiomazine is shown to bind to Adra1d and Adra1a, both of which participate in Alpha1- and Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, respectively. These activities are ultimately linked to Adra1b, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Propiomazine may influence Adra1b function. The evidence indicates that Propiomazine interacts with Adra1d and Adra1a, which are both involved in the same biological pathway, thereby implying a shared role in the regulation of adrenergic receptor activity. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and significant interaction, though the exact nature of the binding and its downstream effects on Adra1b remain to be fully elucidated. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of adrenergic receptor activity through the interaction with these receptor isoforms, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct impact on Adra1b.",
